    Detect musl libc in statically linked binaries (#3798)
    
    The existing musl detection searches `.rodata` for the string
    `"/tmp/tmpnam_XXXX"` (from musl's `tmpnam.c`). This works for
    dynamically linked binaries where the full libc is loaded, but fails
    for statically linked ones — the linker only includes referenced
    code/data, so if the program never calls `tmpnam()`, that string is
    absent.
    
    Add a fallback: search `.rodata` for musl's mallocng `size_classes`
    array, a 96-byte `uint16_t[48]` constant from `malloc.c`. This table
    is linked into any program that calls `malloc()` (nearly all of them),
    and the 96-byte pattern makes false positives essentially impossible.
    Both little-endian and big-endian representations are checked.
    
    This covers musl v1.2.1+ (2020), when the mallocng allocator replaced
    oldmalloc. The same `size_classes` values are already used in
    `pwndbg/aglib/heap/mallocng.py` for heap inspection.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

