    kernel/slab: fix slab list field name for pre-5.8 kernels (#3803)
    
    * kernel/slab: fix slab list field name for pre-5.8 kernels
    
    In kernels older than ~5.8, struct page uses the 'lru' field as the
    linked list head for node partial slabs. The 'slab_list' name was only
    introduced when the slab-specific fields in struct page were explicitly
    named (later backported into struct slab in 5.17).
    
    NodeCache.partial_slabs hardcoded "slab_list" as the field passed to
    container_of(), causing offsetof() to return None on old kernels and
    a TypeError crash:
      unsupported operand type(s) for -: 'int' and 'NoneType'
    
    Fix by probing at runtime whether the slab struct actually has a
    'slab_list' field, falling back to 'lru' if not.
    
    Fixes: slab list crashing on kernel 4.4.x and other pre-5.8 kernels
    
    * Update comment: slab_list was introduced in kernel 4.18, not 5.8

